  [1mMain finding:[0m the repo has a vendored component library in [38;5;153mvendor/kit[39m that already does most of what the page needs.
  Only [38;5;153mbutton[39m and [38;5;153mdialog[39m are used anywhere so far. The plan builds the page from it instead of copying the hand-written
  HTML in [38;5;153mservices.js[39m:
  - [38;5;153mdataTable[39m sorts the rows and draws the sort links with arrows.
  - [38;5;153mfilterBar[39m and [38;5;153mselectField[39m give the dropdown that submits on change and keeps the current sort.
  - [38;5;153mbadge[39m already has green, amber, red and blue styles that fit the four statuses.
  - [38;5;153mpageHeader[39m and [38;5;153memptyState[39m cover the heading and the empty message.

  The query handling ([38;5;153menv[39m, [38;5;153msort[39m, [38;5;153mdir[39m, and falling back on unknown values) copies [38;5;153mservices.js[39m.

  [1mThe two tasks:[0m
  1. [1mThe page itself[0m ([38;5;153msrc/pages/deploys.js[39m), with 10 rendering tests. They cover the snapshot time and column order,
     newest first, both sorts in both directions, the four chip colors, the duration format and "running", the filter,
     the empty message, and unknown query values. The test rows are deliberately out of date order, so the newest-first
     test only passes if the page actually sorts.
  2. [1mRoute, nav link and test data:[0m the [38;5;153m/deploys[39m route, the nav link after "Services", server tests for the page and its
     503, the deploys row in the README's page list, and a [38;5;153mdeploys.json[39m for each of the empty and one-row test data
     sets. Without those two files, the existing tests that open every nav link would fail with a 503 as soon as the
     link exists, so they have to land in the same task.

  [1mChecked:[0m I ran the plan's code and tests in a throwaway copy of the repo. All 392 tests pass (the current 380 plus 12
  new), so the expected markup in each assertion matches what the kit really renders.

  [1mChoices the spec didn't settle, for you to check:[0m
  - [1mDefault sort direction:[0m a link like [38;5;153m?sort=service[39m with no [38;5;153mdir[39m sorts Service A to Z, while Started without a [38;5;153mdir[39m
    stays newest first.
  - [1mEmpty message with "All environments":[0m this only happens when the snapshot itself is empty, and the page then says
    "No deploys".
  - [1mTimestamps[0m stay as raw ISO strings, like the Services and Overview pages do.
  - [1mDuration[0m is a small function inside the page, since nothing in [38;5;153msrc/[39m formats durations yet.

  When you've read it and are happy, tell me to go ahead and I'll run it task by task, with a fresh subagent and a
  review for each task.

